english_text:
Twelve Men Are Sent into Canaan
(Deuteronomy 1.19-33)
1The Lord said to Moses, 2“Choose a leader from each tribe and send them into Canaan to explore the land I am giving you.”
3So Moses sent twelve tribal leaders from Israel's camp in the Paran Desert 4-16with orders to explore the land of Canaan. And here are their names:
Shammua son of Zaccur
from Reuben,
Shaphat son of Hori
from Simeon,
Caleb son of Jephunneh
from Judah,
Igal son of Joseph
from Issachar,
Joshua son of Nun
from Ephraim,
Palti son of Raphu
from Benjamin,
Gaddiel son of Sodi
from Zebulun,
Gaddi son of Susi
from Manasseh,
Ammiel son of Gemalli
from Dan,
Sethur son of Michael
from Asher,
Nahbi son of Vophsi
from Naphtali,
and Geuel son of Machi
from Gad.
17Before Moses sent them into Canaan, he said:
After you go through the Southern Desert of Canaan, continue north into the hill country 18and find out what those regions are like. Be sure to remember how many people live there, how strong they are, 19-20and if they live in open towns or walled cities. See if the land is good for growing crops and find out what kinds of trees grow there. It's time for grapes to ripen, so try to bring back some of the fruit that grows there.
21The twelve men left to explore Canaan from the Zin Desert in the south all the way to the town of Rehob near Lebo-Hamath in the north. 22As they went through the Southern Desert, they came to the town of Hebron, which was seven years older than the Egyptian town of Zoan. In Hebron, they saw the three Anakim clans of Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai. 23-24When they got to Bunch Valley, they cut off a branch with such a huge bunch of grapes, that it took two men to carry it on a pole. That's why the place was called Bunch Valley. Along with the grapes, they also took back pomegranates and figs.
The Men Report Back to the People
25After exploring the land of Canaan for 40 days, 26the twelve men returned to Kadesh in the Paran Desert and told Moses, Aaron, and the people what they had seen. They showed them the fruit 27and said:
Look at this fruit! The land we explored is rich with milk and honey. 28But the people who live there are strong, and their cities are large and walled. We even saw the three Anakim clans. 29Besides that, the Amalekites live in the Southern Desert; the Hittites, Jebusites, and Amorites are in the hill country; and the Canaanites live along the Mediterranean Sea and the Jordan River.
30Caleb calmed down the crowd and said, “Let's go and take the land. I know we can do it!”
31But the other men replied, “Those people are much too strong for us.” 32Then they started spreading rumors and saying, “We won't be able to grow anything in that soil. And the people are like giants. 33 In fact, we saw the Nephilim who are the ancestors of the Anakim. They were so big that we felt as small as grasshoppers.”

translation_text:
Benjaminn aanibol ni aanib bi nan ye David aajan aadidiliib na
1David aah nan san ke u ŋmar Ubɔr Sɔɔl chee, ki ti bi Siklag ni na, le bijab bi nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na pam dan u chee nima. 2Bi nan ye Sɔɔl aado yaab Benjaminn aanibol ni aanib la. Bi nan ŋmaa too ipiin, le ki ŋmaa joo ŋŋangii, ni ŋŋangan mɔmɔk gbaa ŋifulaatan mu pam. 3-7Sema u nyan ni Gibea aatiŋ ni na aajapɔtiib Ahieser ni Joas le nan ye baayidam.
Bijab ngbaan aayimbil sɔ:
Asmafef aajapɔtiib Jesiel ni Pelet.
Beraka, ni Jehu u nyan ni Anatof aatiŋ ni na.
Ismaya u nyan ni Gibeonn aatiŋ ni, ki ye uja u nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na. U nan ye “Piitaa Na” ponn ni aayidaan ubaa la.
Jeremia, ni Jahasiel, ni Johanann, ni Josabad u nyan ni Gedera ni na.
Elusia, ni Jerimof, ni Bealia, ni Semaria, ni Sefatia u nyan ni Harif ni na.
Elkana, ni Isia, ni Asarel, ni Joeser, ni Jasobeam, bi ye Kora aataŋaal pu yaab na.
Jeroham u nyan ni Gedor na aajapɔtiib Joela ni Sebadia.
David aadidiliib bi nyan ni Gad aanibol ni na
8Gad aanibol ni aajab bi nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm ki kpa ŋiyimbil ki nan buen ti kpee David ni waajab pu, buyoonn u nan bi nteersakpiin ni, nin chee bi nan kii mbamɔm na sɔ. Bi nan ye bijab bi nyi tikpaatunn ni kijaak aapen aabɔr sakpen na la. Binimbil wɔb nan kpa ijawaan ke ichinn na la, le bi ŋmaa san ke lijool paab aapeeman na. 9-13Baaninkpir aah nan paa paa tɔb pu pu na sɔ: Eser, ni Obadia, ni Eliab, ni Mismana, ni Jeremia, ni Atai, ni Eliel, ni Johanann, ni Elsabad, ni Jeremia, ni Makbanai.
14Gad aanibol ni aajab bimina bibaa nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋichur aaninkpiib la, le biken mu paa ki ye bijab nkub nkub aaninkpiib. 15Libiln libaa aajan aaŋmal ponn ni, n‑yoonn mu Jɔɔdann Aamɔɔl nyan nwam na, le bi nan puur limɔɔl, le ki ti jenn yaa binib bi bi limɔɔl ngbaan aawipuul ni liwilir mɔk aafatann ni na.
David aadidiliib bi nan nyan ni Benjaminn ni Juda aanibol ni na
16Bijab nan nyan ni Benjaminn ni Juda aanibol ni, ki buen David aah nan bi nin chee bi kii mbamɔm na. 17David nan tooh bi nsan ni le ki ti bui ke, “Ni yaa ye jɔtiib le ki choo ni nan ter mi kan, dan man. Nan kpee ti pu man. Tɔ, maah kaa ŋa nimi nibaa na, ni yaa choo ke ni nan ti di mi kooh maadim pu kan, tiyaajatiib Aawumbɔr ga bee ki ga daa nitafal.”
18Le Uwumbɔr Aafuur Nyaan gbiin bi ponn ni ubaa, u bi yin u ke Amasai na. U nan ŋa “Piitaa Na” aayidaan n‑yoonn mubaa, le u teen ke,
“Jese aajapɔɔn David, ti si aachaŋ ni la.
Linyaŋ ye sin ni binib bi ter si na yaan la.
Uwumbɔr bi aa chee.”
David nan gaa bi iŋaal ilee, le ki ŋa bi bininkpiib waajab ni.
David aadidiliib bi nan nyan ni Manase aanibol ni na
19Manase aanibol ni aajab bibaa nan buen ti kpee David pu, buyoonn u ni Filistia yaab nan cha bi ti faa Ubɔr Sɔɔl butɔb na. Mbamɔn, Filistia aabɔrb nan san ijawaan ke nibaakan David ga di bi kooh waaninkpel Sɔɔl pu, kina le bi nan cha u gir Siklag aatiŋ ni. Kina pu na, David aa nan ter Filistia yaab butɔb ngbaan ni. 20David aah nan gir cha aan bijab bi nan nyan Manase aanibol ni ki dii u na sɔ: Adna, ni Josabad, ni Jediael, ni Maikel, ni Josabad, ni Elihu, ni Siletai. Bi nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋichur aayidam le Manase aanibol ni. 21Baah nan ye bijab bi nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na, bi nan ye David aajab ponn ni bininkpiib la. Puwɔb le bi nan ŋa Israel aajab ponn ni bininkpiib. 22Iwiin mɔmɔk kan, bijab nan moo kpae David aajab pu la, le bi ti wiir ti nyaŋ.
David aajab aakahm
23-37David aah nan bi Hebronn aatiŋ ni na, le bijab bi bae ki nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na dan nan kpee u pu, ke bi nyan Sɔɔl ki di u ŋa ubɔr, Uwumbɔr aah nan puu pu na. Baawiwiir sɔ:
Juda aanibol ni aajab bi nan kpa tijawan mbamɔm na, nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋiloob ni ikui iniin la. Bi mɔmɔk nan kpa kijaak aapen ni tikpaatunn la;
Simeonn aanibol ni aajab bi nan bae ki nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na, nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋilole ni nkub la;
Liifai yaab nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋinaa ni ikui iloob la;
Aaronn aayaabil Jehoyada aadidiliib nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋitaa ni ikui ilole la;
Sadok, u nyi kijaak aabɔr pam na aado yaab nan ye bisalolm moninko ni bilee la;
Benjaminn aanibol, Sɔɔl ubaa aanibol ni aajab nan ye bijab ŋichur ŋitaa la. Benjaminn aanibol ni aanib pam le nan beenin si Sɔɔl aachaŋ ni;
Efraim aanibol ni aajab nan ye bijab ŋichur moninko ni ikui iniin la. Bi mɔmɔk nan ye bijakpaam le baataŋaal ni;
Manase aanibol li bi liwilir wɔb na aajab nan ye bijab ŋichur kipiik ni ŋiniin la. Bi nan lee bi ke bi ti ŋa David ubɔr la;
Isakar aanibol ni bisalolm nan ye ikui ilee la, le ki joo ni baajab kpee; bisalolm bimina le nan nyi Israel yaab aah ga ŋa pu na, ni buyoonn bi ga ŋa kina na;
Sebulunn aanibol ni aajab bi nan bae ki nyi tijawan mɔmɔk aabɔr, aan bi ga ŋmaa nyu bi pu kaafa na, nan ye bijab ŋichur piiŋmu la;
Naftali aanibol ni, bisalolm lichur, ni bijab bi kpa kijaak aapen ni tikpaatunn na, ŋichur piitaa ni ŋilole;
Dann aanibol ni aajab bi nan nyi butɔb aabɔr mbamɔm na nan ye bijab ŋichur moninko ni ŋiniin ni ikui iloob la.
Aser aanibol ni aajab bi nan gor ki kii butɔb na nan ye bijab ŋichur imonko ilee la;
Ŋinibol ŋi bi Jɔɔdann aamɔɔl aawipuul wɔb, ki ye Rubenn, ni Gad, ni Manase aanibol li bi nima na aajab bi bae ki nyi tiwan mɔmɔk aabɔr mbamɔm na, nan ye bijab ŋichur nkub ni moninko la.
38Bijab bee mɔmɔk nan gor ki kii butɔb la, le ki buen David chee Hebronn ni, ki joo gbin gbin ke bi ti ŋa u Israel mɔmɔk aabɔr. Israel aanib bi mɔmɔk nan gur na nan ŋa kimɔbaan, nlandakbaan ngbaan pu la. 39Bi nan ti bi David chee nima ki ti saa iwiin itaa, ki jin tijikaar ni ŋisubil aadaan mu bido yaab nan ŋa tii bi na aajim. 40Binib nan nyan ni Isakar, ni Sebulunn, ni Naftali aanibol ŋi bi ŋŋangan wɔb dandar na, ki joo ni tijikaar ti ye n‑yon, ni ŋikakan, ni ŋisubil ŋi bi den ŋi aan ŋi kuur na, ni ŋisubil aadaan, ni olif aakpan, ibon, ni laakumii tiib, ni tiwakor ti naahn ibon na, ni inaa pu, nan tii bi. Bi nan ki joo ni inaa ni ipiih ke bi nan li kɔr ŋmɔ. Kitiŋ ngbaan mɔmɔk aanib aapopiin mu bi nan kpa na, le bi nan joo mɔk na.

english_text:
David Assigns Army Commanders
1Each month a group of 24,000 men served as soldiers in Israel's army. These men, which included the family leaders, army commanders, and officials of the king, were under the command of the following men, arranged by the month of their service:
2In the first month, Jashobeam the son of Zabdiel, 3a descendant of Perez;
4in the second month, Dodai the Ahohite, whose assistant was Mikloth;
5in the third month, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada the priest, 6who was the leader of the Thirty Warriors, and whose son Ammizabad was also an army commander;
7in the fourth month, Asahel the brother of Joab, whose son Zebadiah took over command after him;
8in the fifth month, Shamhuth from the Izrah clan;
9in the sixth month, Ira the son of Ikkesh from Tekoa;
10in the seventh month, Helez from Pelon in the territory of Ephraim;
11in the eighth month, Sibbecai from Hushah of the Zerah clan;
12in the ninth month, Abiezer from Anathoth in the territory of Benjamin;
13in the tenth month, Maharai from Netophah of the Zerah clan;
14in the eleventh month, Benaiah from Pirathon in the territory of Ephraim;
15in the twelfth month, Heldai from Netophah, who was a descendant of Othniel.
David Assigns Tribal Leaders
16-22Here is a list of the leaders of each tribe in Israel:
Eliezer son of Zichri was over Reuben; Shephatiah son of Maacah was over Simeon; Hashabiah son of Kemuel was over the Levites, and Zadok the priest was over the descendants of Aaron; Elihu the brother of David was over Judah; Omri son of Michael was over Issachar; Ishmaiah son of Obadiah was over Zebulun; Jerimoth son of Azriel was over Naphtali; Hoshea son of Azaziah was over Ephraim; Joel son of Pedaiah was over West Manasseh; Iddo son of Zechariah was over East Manasseh; Jaasiel son of Abner was over Benjamin; Azarel son of Jeroham was over Dan.
23 When David decided to count the people of Israel, he gave orders not to count anyone under 20 years of age, because the Lord had promised long ago that Israel would have as many people as there are stars in the sky. 24 Joab the son of Zeruiah had begun to count the people, but he stopped when the Lord began punishing Israel. So the total number was never included in David's official records.
Officials in Charge of the King's Property
25Azmaveth the son of Adiel was in charge of the king's personal storage rooms. Jonathan the son of Uzziah was in charge of the king's other storerooms that were in the towns, the villages, and the defense towers in Israel.
26Ezri the son of Chelub was in charge of the workers who farmed the king's land.
27Shimei from Ramah was in charge of the vineyards, and Zabdi from Shepham was in charge of storing the wine.
28Baal Hanan from Geder was in charge of the olive and sycamore trees in the western foothills, and Joash was in charge of storing the olive oil.
29Shitrai from Sharon was responsible for the cattle that were kept in Sharon Plain, and Shaphat son of Adlai was responsible for those kept in the valleys.
30Obil the Ishmaelite was in charge of the camels, Jehdeiah from Meronoth was in charge of the donkeys, and Jaziz the Hagrite was in charge of the sheep and goats.
31These were the men in charge of David's royal property.
David's Personal Advisors
32David's uncle Jonathan was a wise and intelligent advisor. He and Jehiel the son of Hachmoni taught David's sons.
33Ahithophel and Hushai the Archite were two of David's advisors. 34Jehoiada the son of Benaiah was the king's advisor after Ahithophel, and later, Abiathar was his advisor.
Joab was commander of Israel's army.

translation_text:
Binib bi nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na sɔ
(Nehemia 7.4-73)
1Binib bi nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na pam le nan nyan ni Babiloŋ aapepel ni, ki buen Jerusalem aatiŋ, ni Juda aatim muken ni, bi mɔmɔk cha bido aatim ni. Ubɔr Nebukadnesar aah nan chur bi tinaagbiir buen Babiloŋ buyoonn na, bi nan gur koo nima la. 2Binib bi nan ye baasalolm na le nan ye Serubabel, ni Josua, ni Nehemia, ni Seraya, ni Reelaya, ni Modekai, ni Bilsann, ni Mispar, ni Bigfai, ni Rehum, ni Baana.
3-20Israel aamaal yaab aataŋaal i nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na aakahm sɔ:
Paros aataŋaal—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni nkub ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bilee;
Sefatia aataŋaal—binib ikui itaa ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bilee;
Ara aataŋaal—binib ikui ilole ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni biŋmu;
Jesua ni Joab aayaabitiib bi ye Pahaf Moab aataŋaal na—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni ikui iniin ni kipiik ni bilee;
Elam aataŋaal—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni piiŋmu ni binaa;
Satu aataŋaal—binib ikui iwae ni imonko ilee ni biŋmu;
Sakai aataŋaal—binib ikui ilole ni imonko itaa;
Bani aataŋaal—binib ikui iloob ni imonko ilee ni bilee;
Bebai aataŋaal—binib ikui iloob ni moninko ni bitaa;
Asgad aataŋaal—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni moninko ni bilee;
Adonikam aataŋaal—binib ikui iloob ni imonko itaa ni biloob;
Bigfai aataŋaal—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni piiŋmu ni biloob;
Adinn aataŋaal—binib ikui inaa ni piiŋmu ni binaa;
Ater u bi nan ki yin u ke Hesekia na aataŋaal—binib imonko inaa ni kipiik ni biniin;
Besai aataŋaal—binib ikui itaa ni moninko ni bitaa;
Jora aataŋaal—binib nkub ni kipiik ni bilee;
Hasum aataŋaal—binib ikui ilee ni moninko ni bitaa;
Gibar aataŋaal—binib imonko inaa ni kipiik ni biŋmu.
21-35Binib bi aayaajatiib nan koo ntim mumina ponn ni na aanib bi mu nan gir ni na sɔ:
Betlehem aatiŋ yaab—binib nkub ni moninko ni bitaa;
Netofa aatiŋ yaab—binib piiŋmu ni biloob;
Anatof aatiŋ yaab—binib nkub ni moninko ni biniin;
Asmafef aatiŋ yaab—binib imonko ilee ni bilee;
Kiriaf Jearim, ni Kefira, ni Beerof aatim yaab—binib ikui ilole ni imonko ilee ni bitaa;
Rama ni Geba aatim yaab—binib ikui iloob ni moninko ni ubaa;
Mikmas aatiŋ yaab—binib nkub ni moninko ni bilee;
Betel ni Ai aatim yaab—binib ikui ilee ni moninko ni bitaa;
Nebo aatiŋ yaab—binib piiŋmu ni bilee;
Magbis aatiŋ yaab—binib nkub ni piiŋmu ni biloob;
Elam aatiŋ kiken na yaab—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni piiŋmu ni binaa;
Harim aatiŋ yaab—binib ikui itaa ni moninko;
Lod, ni Hadid, ni Ono aatim yaab—binib ikui ilole ni moninko ni biŋmu;
Jeriko aatiŋ yaab—binib ikui itaa ni imonko ilee ni biŋmu;
Senaa aatiŋ yaab—binib ŋichur ŋitaa ni ikui iloob ni piitaa.
36-39Bitotoorb aamaal aataŋaal i mu nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na sɔ:
Jesua aayaabitiib aasaloln Jedaya aataŋaal—binib ikui iwae ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bitaa;
Imer aataŋaal—binib lichur ni piiŋmu ni bilee;
Pasur aataŋaal—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni imonko ilee ni bilole;
Harim aataŋaal—binib lichur ni kipiik ni bilole.
40-42Liifai aamaal aataŋaal i mu nan gir ni na sɔ:
Hodafia aayaabitiib Jesua ni Kadmiel aataŋaal—binib imonko itaa ni kipiik ni binaa;
Uwumbɔr Aadichal ni aawangbaab ni bilahngaab bi aayaaja nan ye Asaf na aataŋaal—binib nkub ni moninko ni biniin;
Uwumbɔr Aadichal aakikiib bi aayaajatiib nan ye Salum, ni Ater, ni Talmonn, ni Akub, ni Hatita, ni Sobai na aataŋaal—binib nkub ni piitaa ni biwae.
43-54Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatutum aataŋaal i nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na mu sɔ:
Siha, ni Hasufa, ni Tabaof,
ni Keros, ni Siaha, ni Padonn,
ni Lebana, ni Hagaba, ni Akub,
ni Hagab, ni Samlai, ni Hanann,
ni Gidel, ni Gahar, ni Reaya,
ni Resinn, ni Nekoda, ni Gasam,
ni Usa, ni Pasea, ni Besai,
ni Asna, ni Meunim, ni Nefisim,
ni Bakbuk, ni Hakufa, ni Harhur,
ni Basluf, ni Mehida, ni Hasa,
ni Bakos, ni Sisera, ni Tema,
ni Nesia, ni Hatifa.
55-57Solomonn aatutum aataŋaal i mu nan gir ni na sɔ:
Sotai, ni Hasoferef, ni Peruda,
ni Jaala, ni Dakonn, ni Gidel,
ni Sefatia, ni Hatil,
ni Pokeref‑Hasebaim, ni Ami.
58Uwumbɔr Aadichal ni aatutum, ni Solomonn aatutum aayaabitiib bi nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na yaa ti kpaan kan, bi nan ti saa binib ikui itaa ni imonko inaa ni kipiik ni bilee la.
59-60Delaya, ni Tobia, ni Nekoda aayaabitiib bi nan nyan ni Tel Mela, ni Tel Harsa, ni Kerub, ni Adann, ni Imer aatim ni ki mu gir ni na, nan ye binib ikui iloob ni piiŋmu ni bilee la, bi mu aa nan tee kpa limɔkl li ga mɔk ke bi ye Israel aanib na.
61-62Bitotoorb aataŋaal yee mu aa nan kan limɔkl li ga mɔk ke biyaajatiib nan ye bitotoorb na; ima le nan ye Hobaya, ni Hakos, ni Basilai. Basilai aataŋaal ngbaan aayaaja nan yoor Gilead aatiŋ aaja u bi nan yin u ke Basilai na aabisal, le ki gur joo uchool aayimbil yin ubaa. Baah kaa nan ŋmaa kan itaŋaal ngbaan aayaajatiib aamɔkl na, baa nan di bi kpee bitotoorb pu. 63Juu yaab aayidaan nan bui bi ke baan ŋmaa ji tijikaar ti bi di tii Uwumbɔr ipiin na, see utotoor u ga ŋmaa di tiwan ni bi yin ni ke Urim ni Tumim na mɔk ke bi ga ŋmaa ji ti na bi nima.
64-67Binib bi nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na nan ti saa binib ŋichur imonko ilee ni ŋilee ni ikui itaa ni imonko itaa la.
Baanaagbiib, bijab ni bipiib, nan ti saa binib ŋichur ŋilole ni ikui itaa ni piitaa ni bilole la.
Uwumbɔr Aadichal ni aawangbaab, ni bilahngaab, bijab ni bipiib, nan ti saa binib ikui ilee la.
Itaan nan ti saa itaan ikui ilole ni piitaa ni iloob la.
Tiwakor ti naahn ubon na mu nan ti saa ikui ilee ni imonko ilee ni tiŋmu la.
Laakumii tiib nan ti saa ikui inaa ni piitaa ni biŋmu la.
Ibon nan ti saa ŋichur ŋiloob ni ikui ilole ni moninko la.
68Binib bi nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na aah nan ti fuu Uwumbɔr Aadichal chee, Jerusalem ponn ni na, le itaŋaal ngbaan aasalolm bibaa nan tii ipiin, ke bi ki gir di maa Uwumbɔr Aadichal ngbaan, laah nan puen si nin chee na. 69Bi nan tii baah ga nyaŋ pu na; le ipiin ngbaan nan ti saa salmaa u aanyunyuun ga pii njikaabim kuruwaa ikui iŋmu na, ni tikunabr ti mu aanyunyuun nan ti saa njikaabim kuruwaa ŋichur ŋilee ni ikui iniin na, le bitotoorb aawanpeenkaan mu nan ti saa nkub.
70Bitotoorb, ni Liifai yaab, ni binib ngbaan bibaa nan kal kal Jerusalem, ni kaatingbaan ni; le Uwumbɔr Aadichal ni aawangbaab, ni bilahngaab, ni bikikiib, ni laatutum kal kal ntim mu bi gbɔk Jerusalem na; le Israel yaab bi gur na kal kal biyaajatiib aatim ni.

english_text:
The Families Who Came Back with Ezra
1Artaxerxes was king of Persia when I led the following chiefs of the family groups from Babylonia to Jerusalem:
2-14Gershom of the Phinehas family;
Daniel of the Ithamar family;
Hattush son of Shecaniah of the David family;
Zechariah and 150 other men of the Parosh family, who had family records;
Eliehoenai son of Zerahiah with 200 men of the Pahath Moab family;
Shecaniah son of Jahaziel with 300 men of the Zattu family;
Ebed son of Jonathan with 50 men of the Adin family;
Jeshaiah son of Athaliah with 70 men of the Elam family;
Zebadiah son of Michael with 80 men of the Shephatiah family;
Obadiah son of Jehiel with 218 men of the Joab family;
Shelomith son of Josiphiah with 160 men of the Bani family;
Zechariah son of Bebai with 28 men of the Bebai family;
Johanan son of Hakkatan with 110 men of the Azgad family;
Eliphelet, Jeuel, and Shemaiah who returned sometime later with 60 men of the Adonikam family;
Uthai and Zaccur with 70 men of the Bigvai family.
Ezra Finds Levites for the Temple
15I brought everyone together by the river that flows to the town of Ahava where we camped for three days. Not one Levite could be found among the people and priests. 16So I sent for the leaders Eliezer, Ariel, Shemaiah, Elnathan, Jarib, Elnathan, Nathan, Zechariah, and Meshullam. I also sent for Joiarib and Elnathan, who were very wise counselors. 17Then I sent them to Iddo, the leader at Casiphia, and I told them to ask him and his temple workers to send people to serve in God's temple.
18God was kind to us and caused them to send a skillful man named Sherebiah, who was a Levite from the family of Mahli. Eighteen of his relatives came with him. 19We were also sent Hashabiah and Jeshaiah from the family of Merari along with 20 of their relatives. 20In addition, 220 others came to help the Levites in the temple. The ancestors of these workers had been chosen years ago by King David and his officials, and they were all listed by name.
Ezra Asks the People To Go without Eating and To Pray
21Beside the Ahava River, I asked the people to go without eating and to pray. We humbled ourselves and asked God to bring us and our children safely to Jerusalem with all of our possessions. 22I was ashamed to ask the king to send soldiers and cavalry to protect us against enemies along the way. After all, we had told the king that our God takes care of everyone who truly worships him, but that he gets very angry and punishes anyone who refuses to obey. 23So we went without food and asked God himself to protect us, and he answered our prayers.
The Gifts for the Temple
24I chose twelve of the leading priests—Sherebiah, Hashabiah and ten of their relatives. 25-27Then I weighed the gifts that had been given for God's temple, and I divided them among the twelve priests I had chosen. There were gifts of silver and gold, as well as the articles that the king, his advisors and officials, and the people of Israel had contributed. In all there were: 22 tons of silver; 100 silver articles weighing 70 kilograms; 3.4 tons of gold; 20 gold bowls weighing over 8 kilograms; and 2 polished bronze articles as valuable as gold.
28I said to the priests:
You belong to the Lord, the God of your ancestors, and these things also belong to him. The silver and gold were willingly given as gifts to the Lord. 29Be sure to guard them and keep them safe until you reach Jerusalem. Then weigh them inside God's temple in the presence of the chief priests, the Levites, and the heads of the Israelite families.
30The priests and Levites then took charge of the gifts that had been weighed, so they could take them to the temple of our God in Jerusalem.
The Return to Jerusalem
31On the twelfth day of the first month, we left the Ahava River and started for Jerusalem. Our God watched over us, and as we traveled along, he kept our enemies from ambushing us.
32After arriving in Jerusalem, we rested for three days. 33Then on the fourth day we went to God's temple, where the silver, the gold, and the other things were weighed and given to the priest Meremoth son of Uriah. With him were Eleazar son of Phinehas and the two Levites, Jozabad son of Jeshua and Noadiah son of Binnui. 34Everything was counted, weighed, and recorded.
35Those who had returned from exile offered sacrifices on the altar to the God of Israel. Twelve bulls were offered for all Israel. Ninety-six rams and 77 lambs were offered on the altar, and 12 goats were sacrificed for the sins of the people. 36Some of those who had returned took the king's orders to the governors and officials in Western Province. Then the officials did what they could for the people and for the temple of God.

translation_text:
1Taah maa ligoln ngbaan doo na, le ti di ibisamɔi aajaaleŋ tiib piin, le ki ban Uwumbɔr Aadichal aakikiib kaan, ki kan Lidichal ngbaan ni aalahngaab mu, ki tii Liifai yaab mu baatun. 2M nan ban bijab bilee le ki di siin ke bi li ye Jerusalem aayidam; bima le nan ye nna aabo Hanani, ni Hanania u ye bikikiib aaninkpel na. Hanania nan ye unii u aa ga ŋmaa mak u pu na la, ki ye unii u san Uwumbɔr naah ti sɔ na. 3M nan bui bi ke bi li nyi ki taa piir ibisamɔi ngbaan kichakpinaanyeek ni see nwiin ti puu ki pɔɔk, aan ki ki piin ki laŋ i waahr aan bikikiib nin fii baatuln ni, kijook wɔb. M nan ki bui bi ke bi ban bikikiib, binib bi koo Jerusalem ponn ni na ni, ki tii bi ŋipepel ŋibaa bi li kii; ki ki ban biken mu bi li manni baadichal chee.
Binib bi nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na sɔ
(Esra 2.1-70)
4Jerusalem nan ye kitiŋ ki wiir na la, le binib bi nan koo ki ponn ni na aa tee wiir, le kaadichal mu aa nan kee wiir. 5Uwumbɔr nan cha m ŋa nlandak ke m kuun binib ngbaan, ni baayidam, ni baaninkpiib ki bee baamaal aah ye pu na. M nan kan binib bi nan puen nyan tinaagbiir ni ki kun ni na aayimbil aagbaŋ. Maah nan kan pu na sɔ:
6Baah nan chuu bi buen tinaagbiir ni na pam le nan nyan ni Babiloŋ ki gir ni Jerusalem, ni Juda aatiŋ pu, bi mɔmɔk nan kun baatiyil ponn ni. Baamaal nan koo Babiloŋ ni buyoonn ubɔrkpaan Nebukadnesar nan chur bi tinaagbiir ki di buen nima na la. 7Binib bimina le nan ye baayidam: Serubabel, ni Josua, ni Nehemia, ni Asaria, ni Raamia, ni Nahamani, ni Modekai, ni Bilsann, ni Misperef, ni Bigfai, ni Nehum, ni Baana.
8-25Binib bi nan ye Israel yaab ki gir ni na aayimbil sɔ, mmaal mɔk ni ŋaanib bi nyan tinaagbiir ngbaan ni ki gir ni na:
Paros aamaal ponn ni—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni binib nkub ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bilee;
Sefatia aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui itaa ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bilee;
Ara aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni piiŋmu ni binib bilee;
Pahaf Moab, u nan ye Jesua ni Joab aayaabil na aamaal ponn ni—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni ikui iniin ni kipiik ni biniin;
Elam aamaal ponn ni—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni piiŋmu ni binaa;
Satu aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iniin ni imonko ilee ni biŋmu;
Sakai aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui ilole ni imonko itaa;
Binui aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni imonko ilee ni biniin;
Bebai aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni moninko ni biniin;
Asgad aamaal ponn ni—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni ikui itaa ni moninko ni bilee;
Adonikam aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni imonko itaa ni bilole;
Bigfai aamaal ponn ni—binib ŋichur ŋilee ni imonko itaa ni bilole;
Adinn aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni piiŋmu ni biŋmu;
Ater, u bi nan ki yin u ke Hesekia na, aamaal ponn ni—binib imonko inaa ni kipiik ni biniin;
Hasum aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui itaa ni moninko ni biniin;
Besai aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui itaa ni moninko ni binaa;
Harif aamaal ponn ni—binib nkub ni kipiik ni bilee;
Gibeonn aamaal ponn ni—binib imonko inaa ni kipiik ni biŋmu.
26-38Binib bi aayaajatiib nan koo ntim mue ponn ni na mu nan gir ni:
Betlehem ni Netofa aatim ponn ni—binib nkub ni imonko inaa ni biniin;
Anatof aatiŋ ponn ni—binib nkub ni moninko ni biniin;
Bef Asmafef aatiŋ ponn ni—binib imonko ilee ni bilee;
Kiriaf Jearim, ni Kefira, ni Beerof aatim ponn ni—binib ikui ilole ni imonko ilee ni bitaa;
Rama ni Geba aatim ponn ni—binib ikui iloob ni moninko ni ubaa;
Mikmas aatiŋ ponn ni—binib nkub ni moninko ni bilee;
Betel ni Ai aatim ponn ni—binib nkub ni moninko ni bitaa;
Nebo aatiŋ kiken na ponn ni—binib piiŋmu ni bilee;
Elam aatiŋ kiken na ponn ni—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni piiŋmu ni binaa;
Harim aatiŋ ponn ni—binib ikui itaa ni moninko;
Jeriko aatiŋ ponn ni—binib ikui itaa ni imonko ilee ni biŋmu;
Lod, ni Hadid, ni Ono aatim ponn ni—binib ikui ilole ni moninko ni ubaa;
Senaa aatiŋ ponn ni—binib ŋichur ŋitaa ni ikui iwae ni piitaa.
39-42Bitotoorb aamaal ponn ni aanib bi nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na sɔ:
Jedaya, u nan ye Jesua aayaabil na aamaal ponn ni—binib ikui iwae ni imonko itaa ni kipiik ni bitaa;
Imer aamaal ponn ni—binib lichur ni piiŋmu ni bilee;
Pasur aamaal ponn ni—binib lichur ni ikui ilee ni imonko ilee ni bilole;
Harim aamaal ponn ni—binib lichur ni kipiik ni bilole
43-45Liifai yaab aamaal bi nan nyan tinaagbiir ponn ni ki gir ni na sɔ:
Hodafia aayaabitiib Jesua ni Kadmiel aamaal ponn ni—binib imonko itaa ni kipiik ni binaa;
Uwumbɔr Aadichal ni aalahngaab ni biwangbaab, Asaf aayaabitiib,—binib nkub ni imonko ilee ni biniin;
Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aakikiib, biyaajatiib le nan ye Salum, ni Ater, ni Talmonn, ni Akub, ni Hatita ni Sobai,—binib nkub ni piitaa ni biniin.
46-56Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatutum aamaal bi nan nyan tinaagbiir ponn ni ki gir ni na mu sɔ:
Siha, ni Hasufa, ni Tabaof,
ni Keros, ni Sia, ni Padonn,
ni Lebana, ni Hagaba, ni Salmai,
ni Hanann, ni Gidel, ni Gahar,
ni Reaya, ni Resinn, ni Nekoda,
ni Gasam, ni Usa, ni Pasea,
ni Besai, ni Meunim, ni Nefusesim,
ni Bakbuk, ni Hakufa, ni Hahur,
ni Baslif, ni Mehida, ni Hasa,
ni Bakos, ni Sisera, ni Tema,
ni Nesia, ni Hatifa.
57-59Solomonn aatutum aamaal ponn ni bi mu nan nyan tinaagbiir ponn ni ki gir ni na sɔ:
Sotai, ni Soferef, ni Perida,
ni Jaala, ni Dakonn, ni Gidel,
ni Sefatia, ni Hatil,
ni Pokeref‑Hasebaim, ni Amonn.
60Solomonn aatutum aamaal, ni Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatutum aamaal ponn ni aanib bimɔk nan nyan tinaagbiir ponn ni ki gir ni na yaa kpaan kan, bi ye binib ikui itaa ni imonko inaa ni kipiik ni bilee la.
61-62Delaya, ni Tobia, ni Nekoda aamaal ponn ni aanib bi nan nyan ni Tel Mela, ni Tel Hasa, ni Kerub, ni Adonn, ni Imer aatim ponn ni ki mu nan gir ni na nan ti kpaan binib ikui iloob ni imonko ilee ni bilee la. Bi mu aa nan tee ŋmaa mɔk ke bi ye Israel aanib la.
63-64Bitotoorb aamaal i mu aa nan ŋmaa kan kigbaŋ ki ponn ni biyaajatiib aayimbil bi na: ima le ye Hobaya, ni Hakos, ni Basilai aamaal aanib. Basilai aamaal ngbaan aayaaja nan yoor Gilead aatiŋ aaja u bi nan yin u ke Basilai na aabisal, le ki gur joo uchool aayimbil yin ubaa. Imaal ngbaan ponn ni aanib aah kaa kan kigbaŋ ki ponn ni biyaajatiib aayimbil bi na, baa nan kan nsan ke bi li ye bitotoorb. 65Juu yaab aayidaan nan bui bi ke baan ŋmaa ji tijikaar ti bi di tii Uwumbɔr ipiin na, see utotoor u ga ŋmaa di Urim ni Tumim di ŋaŋ ti ki lik na.
66-69Binib bi nan nyan tinaagbiir ni ki gir ni na nan ti kpaan ŋichur imonko ilee ni ŋilee ni ikui itaa ni imonko itaa la.
Baatutum, bijab ni bipiib mɔmɔk nan ye ŋichur ŋilole ni ikui itaa ni piitaa ni bilole la.
Bi nan ye bilahngaab ni biwangbaab, bijab ni bipiib na mu nan ye binib ikui ilee ni imonko ilee ni biŋmu la.
Itaan mu nan ye ikui ilole ni piitaa ni iloob la.
Tiwakor ti naahn ubon na mu nan ye ikui ilee ni imonko ilee ni tiŋmu la.
Laakumii tiib mu nan ye ikui inaa ni piitaa ni biŋmu la.
Ibon mu nan ye ŋichur ŋiloob ni ikui ilole ni moninko la.
70-72Binib pam le nan too tiwan ki ter Uwumbɔr Aadichal aatoorn pu. Baah nan too pu na sɔ:
Baayidaan nan tii salmaa kuruwaa biniin la, ni kitork aasambil piiŋmu, ni bitotoorb aawanpeenkaan mu ikui iŋmu ni piitaa.
Mmaal mɔk aayidam mu nan tii salmaa kuruwaa nkub ni imonko itaa ni biniin la, ni tikunabr mu kuruwaa lichur ni ikui ilee ni piiŋmu la.
Binib bi gur na mu nan tii salmaa kuruwaa nkub ni imonko itaa ni biniin la, ni tikunabr ti mu ga pii kuruwaa nkub ni imonko ilee na, ni bitotoorb aawanpeenkaan mu imonko itaa ni nilole.
73Bitotoorb, ni Liifai yaab, ni Uwumbɔr Aadichal aakikiib, ni bilahngaab, ni biwangbaab, ni Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatutum, ni binib bibaa, ni Israel yaab bi gur na, nan kal itingbaan, ni ntisakpem mu bi Juda ponn ni na ni la.

Bitotoorb ni Liifai aamaal yaab aayimbil sɔ
1Bitotoorb bimina, ni Liifai yaab bee le nan nyan ni tinaagbiir ponn ni ki dii ni Sealtiel aajapɔɔn Serubabel ni Utotoorninkpel Josua:
Bitotoorb ngbaan aayimbil sɔ:
2-7Seraya, ni Jeremia, ni Esra,
ni Amaria, ni Maluk, ni Hatus,
ni Sekania, ni Rehum,
ni Meremof, ni Ido, ni Ginetoi,
ni Abija, ni Mijaminn, ni Maadia,
ni Bilga, ni Semaya, ni Joyarib,
ni Jedaya, ni Salu, ni Amok,
ni Hilkia, ni Jedaya.
Bijab bee le nan ye bitotoorb biken na aayidam, utotoorninkpel Josua aayoonn.
Liifai yaab aayimbil sɔ:
8Jesua, ni Binui, ni Kadmiel, ni Serebia, ni Juda, ni Matania, le nan ye binib bi gaa ilahn ki dooni Uwumbɔr na aayidam.
9Le Bakbukia, ni Uno, ni Liifai yaab biken na nan keei bi.
Utotoorninkpel Josua aamaal
10Josua le nan ma Joyakim; le Joyakim mu ma Eliasib; le Eliasib mu ma Joyada; 11le Joyada mu ma Jonatann; le Jonatann mu ma Jadua.
Bitotoorb aamaal ponn ni aayidam
12-21Joyakim aah nan ye Utotoorninkpel buyoonn na, bitotoorb bee le nan ye baamaal aayidam:
Seraya aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Meraya;
Jeremia aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Hanania;
Esra aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Mesulam;
Amaria aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Jehohanann;
Maluki aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Jonatann;
Sebania aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Josef;
Harim aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Adna;
Merayof aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Helkai;
Ido aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Sekaria;
Ginetonn aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Mesulam;
Abija aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Sikri;
Miniaminn aamaal ponn ni aayidaan aayimbil aa nan bi
Moadia aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Piltai;
Bilga aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Samua;
Semaya aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Jehonatann;
Joyarib aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Matenai;
Jedaya aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Usi;
Salai aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Kalai;
Amok aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Eber;
Hilkia aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Hasabia;
Jedaya aamaal ponn ni aayidaan nan ye Netanel.
Baah nan ŋmee bitotoorb ni Liifai yaab aamaal aayimbil kigbaŋ ponn ni pu na
22Buyoonn Eliasib, ni Joyada, ni Jonatann, ni Jadua nan bi limɔfal ni ki ye bitotoorninkpiib na, le bi nan ŋmee Liifai yaab aamaal aadichadam ni bitotoorb aamaal aadichadam aayimbil. N‑yoonn ngbaan le Darius nan ye Pesia aabɔrkpaan.
23Liifai yaab aamaal aadichadam ma nan ŋmee baayimbil kigbaŋ ponn ni, ki ti saa buyoonn Eliasib aayaabil Jonatann nan bi na la.
Baah yakr Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatuln pu na
24Hasabia, ni Serebia, ni Jesua, ni Binui, ni Kadmiel le nan yakr Liifai yaab ŋigetek, ŋigetek, le bi tun Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aatuln. Ŋigetek ŋilelee le nan kpaani ki pak Uwumbɔr ki dooni u, ke Uwumbɔr aanii, Ubɔrkpaan David aah nan mɔk ke bi li dooni u pu na.
25Matania, ni Bakbukia, ni Obadia, ni Mesulam, ni Talmonn, ni Akub, bi ye Uwumbɔr Aadichal aakikiib na le nan kii tidir ti ponn ni bi joo tiwan siini aan ti bi Uwumbɔr Aadichal aabisamɔi chee na.
26Binib bee nan bi limɔfal ni buyoonn Josua aajapɔɔn Joyakim, u aayaaja nan ye Jehosadak na, ni n‑yoonn mu uyidaan Nehemia, ni utotoor Esra, u nan bee Nkaal mbamɔm na, nan laa bi limɔfal ponn ni na la.
Nehemia aah di Jerusalem aatiŋ aagoln ŋa Uwumbɔr aaŋaal ni pu na
27Buyoonn bi nan di Jerusalem aatiŋ aagoln ŋa Uwumbɔr aaŋaal ni na, bi nan yin ni Liifai yaab baah bi nin chee na mɔmɔk, ke bi nan kpaan kitork ngbaan, ki li gaa ilahn ki dooni Uwumbɔr, ki gbaa tibar ni ichayakrtuun. 28Liifai yaab aalahngaab ngbaan nan nyan ni baah nan ka ka nin chee ki mann goln Jerusalem na, ni ntim mu bi Netofa chee, 29ni Bef Gilgal, ni Geba, ni Asmafef aatim ni ki nan kpaan Jerusalem ni. 30Bitotoorb ni Liifai yaab nan toor kitork ki nyan bibaa ni binib ngbaan aatunwanbir, le ki ŋa ibisamɔi ni kitiŋ aagoln ngbaan chain.
31M nan kuun Juda aayidam ki ti tɔŋ ligoln ngbaan paab, ki di ŋigetek sakpiin ŋilee ŋa biŋaal ni ke bi di bi chuun mann ligoln ngbaan, ki li joo idoon tii Uwumbɔr.
Njan aagetekr nan di toŋ ŋŋangii wɔb ligoln ngbaan paab ki cha Litapuln Aabisamɔb wɔb. 32Hosaya le nan paa bilahngaab pu, le Juda aayidam ligetekr libaa di paan u pu. 33-35Le Asaria, ni Esra, ni Mesulam, ni Juda, ni Benjaminn, ni Semaya, ni Jeremia bi nan ye bitotoorb ki nan pii kakaan tiib na mu nan paan bi pu, le ki di Jonatann aajapɔɔn Sekaria, u aayaaja nan ye Semaya nan paan. Uyaajatiib biken le nan ye Matania, ni Mikaya, ni Sakur, bi ye Asaf aamaal yaab na. 36Udo yaab Semaya, ni Asarel, ni Milalai, ni Gilalai, ni Maai, ni Netanel, ni Juda, ni Hanani le nan paa u pu; bi mɔmɔk nan joo tiwangbaakaan ni bi ke tiwangbaakaan ni Uwumbɔr aanii Ubɔrkpaan David nan gbaa na. Le Esra u nyi Uwumbɔr aakaal mbamɔm na nan loln ligetekr ngbaan pu nsan. 37Baah nan ti fuu mbisamɔb mu bi yin mu ke Uyayak Aabisamɔb chee na, le bi jon ŋibimbin ŋi cha David Aatiŋ ni na, ki jer David aabɔrnaakook, le ki ti ki tɔŋ ligoln ngbaan paab Nnyun Aabisamɔb chee, mu bi liwipuul wɔb kitiŋ ngbaan pu na.
38Ligetekr li mu nan ki joo idoon tii Uwumbɔr na mu nan di toŋ ŋŋangan wɔb ligoln ngbaan paab, le m di binib ligetekr liken di paan bi pu. Ti nan chuun ti jer kidifɔfɔk ki chee bi ŋani boroboro na, ki ti saa Ligowawaal na chee, 39ki nyan nima ki ti jer Efraim Aabisamɔb, ni Jesana Aabisamɔb, ni Ijan Aabisamɔb, ni Hananel Aadifɔfɔk, ni Nkub Aadifɔfɔk, ki ti saa Ipiih Aabisamɔb. Ti nan ti doo timi aasachuln ngbaan Uwumbɔr Aadichal aabisamɔb chee la.
40-41Kina pu na, ŋigetek ŋilee ngbaan ŋi nan joo idoon tii Uwumbɔr na, nan ti fuu Uwumbɔr Aadichal aapaan ni la.
Le bitotoorb Eliakim, ni Maaseya, ni Miniaminn, ni Mikaya, ni Eliwenai, ni Sekaria, ni Hanania nan bi maagetekr ngbaan ni, ki kpee biyidam bi nan bi m chee na pu, ki pii ikpiin. 42Le Maaseya, ni Semaya, ni Eleasar, ni Usi, ni Jehohanann, ni Malkija, ni Elam, ni Eser nan paa. Jesrahia, u nan ye bilahngaab aaninkpel na, ni waalahngaab nan gaa ilahn mpɔɔn pu.
43Bi nan toor titoor pam liyaadaal ngbaan, le binib ngbaan nan kpa mpopiin sakpen, Uwumbɔr aah nan tii bi mmɔɔn pu na. Bipiib ni mbim mu nan bi njim ngbaan ponn ni, le kifuuk ki bi mɔmɔk nan ŋani na nan buen dandar.
Baah tii Uwumbɔr ipiin pu na
44N‑yoonn ngbaan le bi nan ban bijab kaan kiir tidir ti bi joo tijikaar, ni tiwan niken siini na, ni baah di Uwumbɔr Aadichal aajikaar ti bi too too na di ŋa ti ponn ni na; bi nan di ukpaal mɔmɔk aah tii waajikaar aapiin i na, ni libiln mɔk aajikaabim mu puen biir na, ni ŋisubil ŋi mu puen puir na mu di kpee ti pu. Bijab ngbaan le nan ye bi ga li gaal ikpaakon i bi duun ntim mɔmɔk na, bitotoorb ni Liifai yaab aajikaar ti bi too tii bi, Nkaal aah mɔk pu na nan tii bi. Binib mɔmɔk nan kpa mpopiin bitotoorb ni Liifai yaab ngbaan pu; 45ba pu? bi nan toor titunwanbir aachapinn ni titoor timɔk gur na, Uwumbɔr aah mɔk pu na. Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aalahngaab, ni biwangbaab ni bikikiib mu nan tun baatun ki dii ikaal i Ubɔrkpaan David ni ujapɔɔn Solomonn nan siin na. 46Ki nyan Ubɔrkpaan David ni ulahngaar Asaf aayoonn mu jer na, bilahngaab ni biwangbaab ngbaan le lolni nsan ki pak ki joo idoon tii Uwumbɔr. 47Serubabel aayoonn, ni Nehemia aayoonn na, Israel aanib nan tii iwiin mɔmɔk aajikaar ki joo ter Uwumbɔr Aadichal ponn ni aalahngaab, ni biwangbaab, ni Uwumbɔr Aadichal aakikiib. Binib ngbaan nan ki di tijikaar tii Uwumbɔr, ti li ye Liifai yaab yaan, le bi mu ki lee tii bitotoorb, nkaal aah mɔk pu na.

Nkiirm aameel
1Uwumbɔr, li pel maamɔboln, ki ŋun maah ker idun pu na.
2Maawumbɔr u ye maabɔr na,
li ŋun maah yin si ki ban nterm pu na.
Uwumbɔr, m mee si la;
3aa ŋun maameel kichakpiik ni;
nwiin yaa puu kan, le m di maameel tii si,
ki kii saah ga gar mu pu na.
4Aa ye Uwumbɔr u kaa gee titunwanbir na la;
saa cha kinimbɔŋ duun ni si.
5Aanimbil aa kani bigaadam; saa gee bibiindam.
6Aa bii binyamɔndam mɔmɔk doo
ki lik seeni binib bi bir ki ŋmanni biken na.
7Le saageehm sakpem pu
m ga ŋmaa koo ni Saadichal ni;
m ga ŋmaa doon si Saadichal li bi chain na ponn ni,
ki di kipak gbaan aanimbiin ni.
8Uwumbɔr, m kpa bidim sakpen a.
Mɔk mi saageehn, ki cha m bee saalandak ki dii mu.
9Maan kii tii maadim aah len pu na;
bi ban bi li bii baanja la.
Baamɔliin mɔ le ki joon;
le ki tee gbii ŋŋmann mu ga ku na.
10Uwumbɔr, bii baabɔr ki daa bitafal;
cha bibaa aakpokl ku bi doo.
Baatunwanbir sakpenn, ni baah yii saamɔb pu na,
jenn nyan bi aanimbiin ni.
11Le binib bi kan ŋŋmarm aa chee na ma ga li mɔɔni;
bi ga ŋmaa gaa ilahn mpopiin pu n‑yoonn mɔmɔk.
Li kii binib bi mɔmɔk gee si na;
ba pu? sin pu le bi kpa mpopiin bamɔnn.
12Uwumbɔr, aa ŋani tinyoor ŋani bi keei saamɔb na pu;
le saageehm kii bi ke kijaak aapeln na.

Uwumbɔr le ye ujojoorkpaan
1Uwumbɔr le ye paacham aaninkpiib aakuun ni aayidaan;
bitinjoob aakuun ni, u tii bi waalandak ke,
2“Di cha nimi aabamɔn gangal ngbaan aabɔjil;
taa ki joo ibamɔn tii bibiindam man.
3Cha bigiim ni nkpobim kan baabamɔn;
cha binib bi kaa kpa na,
ni binib bi kaa kpa biteterb na kan baabamɔn.
4Nyan bi titunwanbirdam aapɔɔn ni man.
5Naa nyi nibaa. Ni ye bijɔrb la.
Ni sil ye bijinjirb la, le ibamɔn san dulnyaa wee ni.
6M bui ke, ‘Ni ye maabim la;
ni mɔmɔk ye Min Uwumbɔr u kaa kpa ŋeen aatɔ na aajapɔtiib la.’
7Tɔ, ni mu ga kpoi ke unibɔn na la;
nimɔfal ga doo ke uyidaan mɔk aah ga doo pu na la.”
8Uwumbɔr, dan, ki nan joo dulnyaa;
ŋitimbol mɔmɔk ye sin yaan la.

Uninyaan aapopiin
1Pak Uwumbɔr man.
Unii umɔk nyuŋni Uwumbɔr
ki gee ke u li joo waakaal na kpa mpopiin.
2Uninyaan aabim ga li kpa mpɔɔn kitiŋ pu;
uyaabitiib ga kan tinyoor.
3Waadichal ga li kpa liwangol ni ŋimombil,
le u ga li ye uwankpadaan n‑yoonn mɔmɔk.
4Bininyaam yaa bi mbɔmbɔɔn ni kan, ni ye nwiihn ŋmeen la;
ni ye nwiihn ki tii binib bi san kinimbaak,
ki kpa tiŋann, ki si chob na.
5Unii u pinn biken tiwan, kaa san ijawaan,
kaa kpa beebee waatuln ni na kpa mpopiin.
6Uninyaan aan ŋmaa lir daalbaadaal;
bi ga li teer u bɔr n‑yoonn mɔmɔk.
7Bi yaa tuk u nsuubiin aabɔr kan, naa chur u ijawaan;
u kpa gaakii u pɔɔ na, le ki kpa Uwumbɔr pu limakl.
8Waa san ijawaan, le nibaa aa muk u;
u ga sil kan ke waadim lir.
9U tii binib bi kaa kpa na, ni usui mɔmɔk la,
le waaŋann aa kpa ndoon;
u ga li kpa mpɔɔn ni kipak.
10Bibiindam kani kina, le baaŋuul fiir;
bi gbee ŋiningbee le ki siir mala;
baamakl mɔmɔk doo a.

Idoon aalahn
1Uwumbɔr ŋan, kina pu na, doon u man;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
2Di idoon tii Uwumbɔr u jer ŋiwaa mɔmɔk na;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
3Di idoon tii Uwumbɔr u jer dindatiib mɔmɔk na;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
4Uma baanja le tun iwaan aatukpaan;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
5U di waalan le naan paacham;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
6U maa kitiŋ tɔŋ nnyun mu nyoo na pu;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
7U naan nwiin ni uŋmal;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon;
8ke nwiin li wiin nwiin pu;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon
9ke uŋmal ni iŋmabi li wiin kinyeek;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
10U nan ku Ijipt yaab aajan aabijabim;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
11U nan nyan Israel yaab Ijipt aatiŋ ni;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
12U nan di waaŋaal mu kpa mpɔɔn sakpen na le ŋa kina;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
13U nan chuu yakr Limɔɔkal Aanyusakpem nfum mulee;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
14U nan di waanib dii nima jer;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon;
15le ki tee cha Ijipt aabɔr ni waajab bee Nnyusakpem ngbaan ni;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
16U nan di waanib bɔ dii nteersakpiin ni;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
17U ku bibɔrb bi kpa mpɔɔn na;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
18U ku bibɔrkpaam;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
19U ku Amor yaab aabɔr Sihonn;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
20U ku Basann aatiŋ aabɔr Og;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
21U nan di baatim tii waanib Israel yaab;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
22U nan di mu tii waatutunn Israel aatimbol;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
23Bidim aah nyaŋ timi na, waa nan suln ti bɔr;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
24U nan gaa timi, timi aadim chee lii;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
25U tii tiwanfuurkaan mɔmɔk tijikaar;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.
26Di idoon tii Uwumbɔr u bi paacham na man;
waageehm aa kpa ndoon.

Nkiirm aameel
1Uwumbɔr, gaa mi titunwanbirdam chee lii;
nyan mi binib bi aabimbin pɔɔ na chee.
2N‑yoonn mɔmɔk kan, bi kpokl titunwanbir la,
bi ban kijaak n‑yoonn mɔmɔk la.
3Bilambil bi ke uwaa u kpa liluul na la;
baamɔbon kpa liluul ke saapa aaluul na la.
4Uwumbɔr, li kii mi, aan m taa koo bibiindam aapɔɔn ni;
nyan mi binib bi aabimbin pɔɔ aan bi kpokl n‑yoonn mɔmɔk
ki ban maalirm na aaŋaal ni,
5Binib bi kpa kigaak na pen mi kitaŋ; bi pen kakpalkaa mam,
le ki pen gaawɔb mam nsan ni kiir mi.
6M bui Uwumbɔr ke, “Sin le ye Maawumbɔr,”
Uwumbɔr, ŋun maah wii ki ban nterm pu na.
7Ndindaan Uwumbɔr, u ye maakikiir, ki ye mpɔɔndaan na,
aa kiir mi butɔb ni.
8Uwumbɔr, taa tii bibiindam baah ban pu na;
taa cha baah kpokl pu na tun lituln.
9Taa cha maadim kan linyaŋ;
cha baah faani mi pu na gir lir bi pu;
10Cha mmiisakɔn mu kpa mmii na lir bi pu;
cha bi di bi mee ŋa mbuu mu ponn ni baan ki ŋmaa nya ni na.
11Taa cha binib bi geei inyamɔn paani biken na kan baah ban pu na;
cha tibɔbir lir binib bi aabimbin pɔɔ na pu ki kuln bi.
12Uwumbɔr, m nyi ke aa ter bigiim baabɔr ni,
ki tii maa‑kpa‑dam baabamɔn.
13Binib bi aabimbin ŋan na ga sil pak si;
bi ga li bi aanimbiin ni la.

1Min Pɔɔl nin Silasi nin Timoti;
Le sɔb kugbɔŋ nan ki tenn Tesalonika a wonjiɛm a laguŋ kan wee ti Baa Uwonbɔr nin ti yudaau Yisa Masiya ye-n;
Uwonbɔr a kaar nin nposɔɔn li be nin ni.
Tesalonika yaab a yada nin bi binbem a bɔr
2Ti le poor Uwonbɔr le ni biɛn nan bu, ki tiɛr ni bu ti wonmiɛlin. 3Ti tiɛr ni bu ti Baa Uwonbɔr ban, ni yada a ŋaam nin ni jiɛm a toon nin ni tama kan wee ni jɔɔ nin ti Yudaau Yisa Masiya nbu le che ni si nbamɔm. 4Ti nabum, ti nyi ke ni ye ban wee Uwonbɔr ban le, ki gann ni ki ta ni ŋa U ninfob, 5nan bu-n tibɔŋann tan foon ni ban nin, kaa nan ye imɔleen a binba, amaa ti nan jɔɔ npɔɔn le nin Kasi a Naaŋ. Le ban nan mɔɔn ti-n chee ti nin yada. Taah nan be ni ban nin, ni nan nyi ti binbem kaah ye man nim bu. 6Ni nan toog tim nin ti Yudaau a binbem le; nin naah nan ji fala kan nin biɛn yɔli, ni nan gaa tibɔŋann nmɔn le nin npopeen man wee Kasi a Naaŋ ta sei ni-n. 7Ni ma bu le che nim kpann limagil ki sei biwonjiɛm ban biɛn be Masedoniya nin Akaya a timin. 8Ti yudaau a bɔŋann nmɔn kaa nan nyan ni ban ki kɔɔ Masedoniya nin Akaya a binba le, amaa naah ŋa Uwonbɔr yada kan nin pii kɔɔ ilog nan biɛn na. Ni ma bu naa ji kpaan ti pag ni ki kpiɛ, 9bininfobin biɛn pag ki jiin naah nan gaa ti man, taah nan dan ni ban n-yonn man nin, nin naah nan jiɛn ni bawoli ki dan Uwonbɔr ban man, ke ni jiɛn Uma ibamɔn a Wonbɔru wan fo-n, 10ki li guu U bija wan yin nyann papaab ki dan nin, wan wee U fiin nkumin nin, Uma ye Yisa wan nyan ti Uwonbɔr a ŋuufiiŋ kan chaan nin yaan.
